{number: 79}
{title: A Mighty Fortress Is Our God}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
A [C] mighty [G] fortress [C] is our [F] God,
A [C] bulwark [G7] never [C] failing;
Our Helper He, a-[G] mid the [F] flood
Of [C] mortal [G7] ills pre-[C] vailing:
For [Am] still our [G] ancient [C] foe
Doth [F] seek to [C] work us [G] woe;
His [Am] craft and [G] pow'r are [C] great,
And, [F] armed with [C] cruel [G] hate,
On [Am] earth is [G] not his [C] e-[F]-[C] [G7]-[C] qual.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Did [C] we in [G] our own [C] strength con-[F] fide,
Our [C] striving [G7] would be [C] losing;
Were not the right Man [G] on our [F] side,
The [C] Man of [G7] God's own [C] choosing:
Dost [Am] ask who [G] that may [C] be?
Christ [F] Jesus, [C] it is [G] He;
Lord [Am] Saba-[G] oth, His [C] Name,
From [F] age to [C] age the [G] same,
And [Am] He must [G] win the [C] bat-[F]-[C] [G7]-[C] tle.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
And [C] though this [G] world, with [C] devils [F] filled,
Should [C] threaten [G7] to un-[C] do us,
We will not fear, for [G] God hath [F] willed
His [C] truth to [G7] triumph [C] through us:
The [Am] Prince of [G] Darkness [C] grim,
We [F] tremble [C] not for [G] him;
His [Am] rage we [G] can en-[C] dure,
For [F] lo, his [C] doom is [G] sure,
One [Am] little [G] word shall [C] fell [F]-[C] [G7]-[C] him.
{end_of_verse}
